<h2>Biography</h2>
<h3>Pawel Osmolski shows exceptional versatility in musical style and production</h3>
<h3>Pawel is always willing to tackle new projects and challenges, so if you're looking for a dedicated music composer with eclectic taste, or a sound designer who pays careful attention to detail, please <a href="http://www.pawel-osmolski.com/?page=compositions">listen</a> to Pawel's music portfolio and <a href="&#109;ailto:pawel&#64;pawel-osmolski&#46;com">contact him</a> to discuss what you need.</h3>
<p>Pawel Filip Osmolski (born May 12, 1983) is an English composer and child prodigy. He started composing on the piano at the age of 7, and was also writing music on the Commodore Amiga computer using <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_tracker" target="_blank">MOD Tracker software</a>. During his teens, he became fascinated with learning the Acoustic/Electric guitar, Bass guitar and Drums, which led him to progress from old school Trackers onto MIDI and Audio workstations such as Avid Pro Tools and Steinberg Cubase.</p>
<div><a href="images/magazine/pawel_nme.jpg" class="highslide" onclick="return hs.expand(this)"><img src="images/magazine/pawel_nme_thumb.jpg" alt="Pawel Osmolski in the NME Magazine" width="262" height="130" class="right" border="0" /></a>
  <div class="highslide-caption"><span class="caption">Source: NME Magazine, New Musical Express</span></div>
</div><p>His musical family meant that he grew up listening to, and playing, all kinds of music, developing strong song-writing individualism and instrumental flexibility. He is an improviser at heart, being able to create melodies and sounds without the need of any significant influence or stimulus.</p>
<p>Pawel was taught privately by a professor of music whilst he attended secondary school, but eventually took his skills further by studying for an Advanced Diploma at The Power House Guitar Institute &amp; Basstech, then for a Bachelor of Arts degree in Music Technology and a Master's degree in Audio Technology. He&rsquo;s the kind of guy that will say  &quot;Bass-boost is only for parties&quot; and &quot;Can I get that in 24-bit please?&quot;</p>
<p>He gained recognition in the media from his well-received <a href="http://www.pawel-osmolski.com/radiohead-remixes/" target="_blank">remixes</a> of Radiohead&rsquo;s unreleased material, and was listed in the Q Magazine, <a href="http://www.mtv.com/news/articles/1484465/20040120/outkast.jhtml" target="_blank">MTV News</a>,  and had an exclusive article printed in the <a href="http://www.nme.com/news/radiohead/17031" target="_blank">NME</a>. Pawel is also known for his contributions to the <a href="http://www.remix64.com/act/devilhood/" target="_blank">Remix64</a> community and <a href="http://pawel-osmolski.bandcamp.com/album/space-explorer-polaris" target="_blank">Chiptune</a> scene, which were done out of his love for 8-bit music and the Commodore 64.</p>
<p>Currently, he is the lead singer-songwriter and producer for the London based unsigned indie band <a href="http://www.crunchalias.com/" target="_blank">CrunchAlias</a>, whilst at the same time recording solo material, collaborating online with other musicians, and actively working on film and video game projects through his audio agency <a href="http://www.crownandcraft.com" target="_blank">Crown &amp; Craft</a>. Pawel goes by the names <a href="http://www.devilhood.com" target="_blank">deVilhoOD</a> and Captain Star Paw, as pseudonyms for releasing his own solo material.</p>
<p>Pawel has always had an avid enthusiasm to explore all approaches to sound and music. He expresses a wide sonic palette, hoping that it will influence and bring inspiration to others.</p>